  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist on the Kibana instance.\n\n**Data exploration:** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has `timestamp` as its time field. The key fields are `response` (text, with a `response.keyword` subfield for exact status codes), `clientip`, `bytes`, `request`, `url`, `agent`, and `geo.*`.\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-650e59f8 Web logs overview` (id `eff-650e59f8-web-logs-overview-3ac970442954`) has five panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (area chart, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n- Responses by status code (bar chart, top 10 values of `response.keyword`)\n\nIts time range is the last year.\n\n**Alert rule:** `EFF-650e59f8 5xx spike` (id `148b3079-e683-4718-87ec-cc8c76dab8dc`) is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`:\n- Matches `response.keyword` with the wildcard `5??`, which covers 500\u2013599.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10 over a 5-minute window.\n- Runs every minute.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- **Enabled:** I enabled the rule so it actually runs. The tool creates rules disabled by default.\n- **No action connector:** The rule has no notification action, so a firing alert only shows in Stack Alerts.\n- **Time range:** I used `now-1y` because I couldn't confirm the sample data's timestamps. If the data is older than a year, the dashboard panels will look empty.\n\n**Not verified:** The Kibana instance doesn't expose direct search or ES|QL endpoints to me, so I couldn't check the actual counts. The rule's status reads `ok` after creation, but I haven't seen it evaluate real 5xx traffic.",
